<title>USA: Kantor - dollar has not hurt US car sales to Japan.</title>
<headline>Kantor - dollar has not hurt US car sales to Japan.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Commerce Secretary Mickey Kantor said Tuesday the recent strength of the dollar against the yen appears not to have hurt U.S. car sales to Japan.</p>
<p>&quot;It appears not to have had any adverse effect whatsoever on our ability to sell cars,&quot; Kantor said at a news conference in answer to a question about the dollar's recent strength.</p>
<p>He said he would not discuss exchange rates.</p>
</text>
